hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"229","Muhammad bin Maimun told us, Yahya told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “was He goes around his wives in one bath.” Abu Bakr said: This is strange news, and what is well known is on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas."
"230","Muhammad ibn Rafi’, Muhammad ibn Yahya, and Ahmad ibn Sa’id al-Rabbati told us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, about Qatada, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to perform one ritual ablution over his wives,” but Al-Rabati said: On the authority of Muammar, and he said: “He goes around.”"
"231","Narrated by Muhammad bin Mansour, the Meccan passport, by Muadh, meaning Ibn Hisham. My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He used to go about his wives every hour of the day and night with one washing, and there were eleven of them,” he said: So I said: To Anas: Was he able to do that? He said: We were talking about the fact that he was given the strength of thirty men."
